    "abstract": "Mask R-CNN extends Faster R-CNN by adding a branch for predicting an object mask in parallel with the existing branch for bounding box recognition, efficiently detecting objects while generating a high-quality segmentation mask for each instance. It is simple to train, adds a small overhead, runs at 5 fps, and generalises to other tasks such as human pose estimation. It outperforms all existing single-model entries on every COCO 2016 challenge task.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "A parallel fully convolutional mask branch on each RoI turns Faster R-CNN into an instance segmentation system with small overhead.",
      "RoIAlign removes the harsh quantisation of RoIPool and substantially improves mask accuracy.",
      "Decoupling mask and class prediction (per-class binary masks with sigmoid BCE, no inter-class competition) is essential.",
      "Mask R-CNN with ResNeXt-101-FPN reaches 37.1 mask AP and 39.8 box AP on COCO test-dev, running at about 5 fps."
    ],
